==English==
{{wikipedia|lang=en}}

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|la|en}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{m|grc|πρόσθεσις||addition}}, from {{m|grc|προστίθημι||I add}}, from {{m|grc|πρός||towards}} + {{m|grc|τίθημι||I place}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*próti}}, {{m|ine-pro|*préti}} + {{m|ine-pro|*dʰédʰeh₁-||to be putting, to be placing}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|prostheses}}

# {{context|medicine|lang=en}} An artificial [[replacement]] for a body part, either internal or external.
# {{context|linguistics|prosody|lang=en}} [[prothesis]]

